      "body": "## Purpose\n\n`Counter(start=N).reset()` in `vllm/utils/counter.py` resets the counter to `0` instead of `N`, so a counter built with a non-zero start loses its offset after a reset. The fix stores `start` and resets to it. The default `start=0` behaves exactly as before, so existing callers (`LLM`, offline entrypoints) are unaffected.\n\n`vllm/utils/counter.py` had no tests, so I added `tests/utils_/test_counter.py`:\n- `test_counter_reset_restores_start`: reproduces the bug (fails on main, passes with this change)\n- `test_atomic_counter_concurrent_inc_dec`: checks that `AtomicCounter` stays consistent under concurrent `inc`/`dec` across 8 threads, which is the reason it holds a lock\n\n## Duplicate check\n\n- `gh search prs --repo vllm-project/vllm --state open \"AtomicCounter\"`: only #31489 (unrelated LoRA change)\n- `gh search prs --repo vllm-project/vllm --state open \"utils counter\"`: no results\n\n## Test plan / results\n\n```text\n$ .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/utils_/test_counter.py -v\ntest_counter_reset_restores_start PASSED\ntest_atomic_counter_concurrent_inc_dec PASSED\n2 passed\n\n# same test file against unmodified main:\nFAILED tests/utils_/test_counter.py::test_counter_reset_restores_start\n1 failed, 1 passed\n\n$ ruff check / ruff format --check (v0.14.0, pre-commit version): passed\n```\n\nCPU only. No model output is affected.\n\nAI assistance was used; I reviewed every changed line and ran the tests above.\n",
