    {
      "body": "Hi @taneem-ibrahim @noooop — this is a small Counter.reset() bugfix (docs/tests not involved in the logic change). pre-run-check is blocking full CI for me as a new contributor.\n\nWould one of you mind commenting `/ci run` when you have a moment (same as you kindly did on #64170)? Happy to address any review feedback. Thanks!",
      "created_at": "2026-10-29T08:24:26Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/64171#issuecomment-6491706848",
      "id": 6491706848,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-29T08:24:26Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "bantianyue"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "What bug is this actually fixing?",
      "created_at": "2026-10-29T19:36:51Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/64171#issuecomment-6506514099",
      "id": 6506514099,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-29T19:36:51Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "njhill"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Thanks for taking a look, @njhill. To be upfront: it's a latent inconsistency rather than a bug any current caller hits. `Counter.__init__` accepts `start`, but `reset()` hard-codes `0`, so `Counter(start=5)` would restart at 0 after a reset. As far as I can tell, every in-tree user of `vllm.utils.counter.Counter` uses the default `start=0`, so nothing changes in behavior today.\n\nThe new test also adds the first coverage for `AtomicCounter` under concurrent `inc`/`dec`. If you think this isn't worth carrying, I'm happy to close it. Thanks!\n",
      "created_at": "2026-10-30T00:52:42Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/64171#issuecomment-6512183253",
      "id": 6512183253,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-30T00:52:42Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "bantianyue"
      }
    }
